User Story 1: Merchant Account Creation
ID: SA-01
Priority: High
Risk: Low
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As a staff member (admin), I want to register a new merchant pharmacy with their business details, so that they can begin using the system to place orders

Acceptance Criteria:
System must capture: merchant name, unique business ID, registered address, and contact email
System must prevent the creation of a merchant with a duplicate business ID or email
Upon creation, the merchant account status must default to "pending" until a credit limit is assigned
All data must be persisted in the central SQL database

User Story 2: Credit Limit Assignment
ID: SA-02
Priority: High
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 3 Story Points

Narrative: As a financial administrator, I want to set a specific credit limit for a merchant account, so that the system can restrict orders once their debt threshold is reached

Acceptance Criteria:
System must allow a user to search for a merchant and input a numerical credit limit
System must reject any negative values for the credit limit
When a credit limit is saved, the system must log the date of the change and the ID of the staff member who made the update
System must provide an interface so the CA subsystem can check this limit before allowing an order


User Story 3: Product Catalogue Management
ID: SA-03
Priority: High
Risk: Low
Estimate: 8 Story Points

Narrative: As an inventory manager, I want to add and update pharmaceutical products in the central catalogue, so that the merchant and public apps have access to up to date item data

Acceptance Criteria:
System must allow editing of the Item name, SKU, bulk price, and stock level
System must support the bulk update of prices for a group of selected items
Prices must be stored to two decimal places to reflect currency standards
System must immediately update the data available to the PU and CA subsystems via the shared interface

User Story 4: Automated Order Validation
ID: SA-04
Priority: High
Risk: High
Estimate: 13 Story Points

Narrative: As the SA subsystem, I want to validate incoming orders from the CA subsystem against current stock and credit levels, so that invalid or high risk orders are rejected before processing

Acceptance Criteria:
System must receive an order object containing merchant ID, item IDs, and quantities
System must verify that the requested quantities are currently in stock before approving
System must verify that the order total does not exceed the merchant's remaining credit limit
System must return a success or failure status code to the CA subsystem within two seconds


User Story 5: Financial Payment Processing
ID: SA-05
Priority: Medium
Risk: Medium
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As an accounting staff member, I want to log payments received from merchants, so that their current debt is reduced and their purchasing power is restored

Acceptance Criteria:
System must provide a searchable list of merchants with outstanding balances
Staff member must be able to select a payment type: Bank Transfer, Card, or Cheque
System must update the merchant's current debt in real-time after the payment is saved
System must generate a unique payment confirmation reference number for auditing

User Story 6: Management Inventory Reporting
ID: SA-06
Priority: Low
Risk: Low
Estimate: 5 Story Points

Narrative: As a warehouse supervisor, I want to generate a report showing items with stock below the reorder threshold, so that I can initiate restocking from suppliers

Acceptance Criteria:
Report must list all items where current stock is below a predefined Reorder Threshold
Report must display Item Name, SKU, Current Stock, and Suggested Reorder Quantity
User must be able to export this report as a PDF or view it on-screen
Report must be timestamped with the current server time and date
